    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43911" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">serrātus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		serra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sawshaped</i>, <i>serrated</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 61, § 160</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">folia herbae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					25, 8, 46, § 84</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambitus (foliorum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					25, 6, 30, § 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
					59, 85, § 182</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compages (ossium capitis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 37, 48, § 132</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morsus (anseris),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 136, 4</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">serrā-ti</span></b> ,
				ōrum (sc. nummi), <i>silver coins notched on the edge</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. G. 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; cf. Eckh. Doctr. Num. 5, p. 94
			sq.</div>
